<title>USA: Kansas City trusts file $300 mln preferred.</title>
<headline>Kansas City trusts file $300 mln preferred.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>KCPL Financing I and two other trusts formed by Kansas City Power and Light Co filed Wednesday with the Securities and Exchange Commission to offer up to $300 million in preferred securities.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the offering will be used to purchase an equivalent of junior subordinated debentures of Kansas City Power.</p>
<p>The parent will use funds it receives from the sale of the debentures for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
</text>
